title: "pallet-broker: keep the existential deposit in the pot"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      The broker pot is now endowed with the existential deposit at genesis, and everything paid
      out of it preserves it. Before, the pot only got a provider reference, so paying out the
      system share of the on-demand revenue could leave less than the existential deposit in it,
      and the private contributors' share was dusted while still recorded as claimable.

      Runtimes using `pallet-broker` must add `pallet_broker::migration::MigrateV5ToV6<Runtime>`
      to their migrations. It mints into the pot whatever it lacks of the existential deposit and
      of the revenue still owed to the private contributors to the Instantaneous Coretime Pool.
  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |
      Private contributors to the Instantaneous Coretime Pool can claim their share of the
      on-demand revenue even when it is below the existential deposit.
crates:
  - name: pallet-broker
    bump: minor
  - name: coretime-westend-runtime
    bump: patch
